Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3 critical structural bugs found and fixed:

1. Embeddings not persisted → Tier 2 resolution 100% dead on resume
   - All 2566 entities had embedding=None after loading from JSON
   - Added _recompute_missing_embeddings() at pipeline start
   - Batch-computes embeddings in groups of 100

2. find_by_name crosses type boundaries via alias index
   - State changes applied to wrong entity through alias collisions
   - Added entity_type parameter to find_by_name for type-safe lookups
   - Pipeline now checks batch-local name_to_id before falling back

3. Context preamble leaks aliases → extraction hint cascade
   - LLM sees aliases, writes matches_existing pointing to aliases
   - Wrong alias indexed → cascade of bad merges
   - Removed aliases from preamble output

Entity resolver hardening (5 fixes):
- Extraction hint path: cross-type → LLM verify (was blindly trusting)
- String match >=0.90 auto-accept now requires same type
- Cross-type string match → LLM verify instead of auto-accept
- Always filter by type (removed concept exception)
- Stricter LLM verify prompt ("when in doubt, answer no")

World model fixes:
- Containment check: min 4 chars, 30% length ratio, capped at 0.87
- add_alias: max 10 aliases, word-overlap validation
- add_relationship: dedup by (source_id, target_id, type)
- Added remove_alias, get_entities_without_embeddings, set_entity_embedding

New tools:
- tools/backfill.py: clean aliases, dedup transitions, importance scores, embeddings
- briefing.py: daily briefing generator
- mcp_server.py: MCP server for PIE integration
- explorer.html: interactive world model explorer

